14. Unified HTML Report

Do NOT create completely separate test systems or separate competing reports.

Use:

«One migration test harness + one unified test model + one overall HTML report.»

However, the HTML report should keep validation concerns clearly separated.

Example:

SIT-0234 Customer Load
================================================

OVERALL RESULT: PASS

1. Assertions
------------------------------------------------
[PASS] 10,000 records processed
[PASS] Output file exists
[PASS] Workflow successful

2. Hop Execution
------------------------------------------------
[PASS] Workflow started
[PASS] Pipeline A executed
[PASS] Pipeline B executed
[PASS] Workflow completed

3. Pentaho <-> Hop Comparison
------------------------------------------------
[SEMANTIC MATCH] Job -> Workflow
[SEMANTIC MATCH] Transformation -> Pipeline
[EXACT MATCH]    Records processed

4. Evidence
------------------------------------------------
Pentaho evidence       | Hop evidence
-----------------------|-------------------------
Job started            | Workflow started
Transformation A       | Pipeline A
10000 records          | 10000 records
Job completed          | Workflow completed

The user should see one authoritative result.

The underlying engines remain modular.

