16. CI/CD Integration

The existing Pentaho process fails the Jenkins build when tests fail.

The Hop validation framework should preserve that contract.

Recommended pipeline:

Jenkins
   |
   v
Build Hop project/image
   |
   v
Prepare test environment
   |
   v
Run migration test suite
   |
   v
Execute Hop workloads
   |
   v
Capture evidence
   |
   v
Evaluate assertions
   |
   v
Generate HTML report
   |
   v
Generate JUnit XML
   |
   v
Return process exit code

Result:

exit 0
    -> Jenkins PASS

non-zero
    -> Jenkins FAIL

---

17. JUnit XML

The harness should generate JUnit-compatible XML even though the tests do not need to be implemented using JUnit internally.

Example conceptual result:

Tests: 250
Passed: 249
Failed: 1
Skipped: 0

Jenkins can consume the report using standard test reporting.

This gives the migration test harness standard enterprise CI behaviour without requiring Hop workflows themselves to implement JUnit.

